This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

**Session context**: This is a continuation of a previous session where the initial version of Getnet Demil Jenberia's portfolio was built at `/scratch/gdemil24/getnet-demil.github.io/`. The user requested a comprehensive redesign of that site with the following explicit requirements:

1. **Visit old website** `getnetdemil.github.io` to extract ALL content (it's a React SPA inside the new repo as a subfolder)
2. **Beautiful timeline designs** for news, education, and career sections
3. **"See more" smart buttons** for long sections
4. **LinkedIn post integration** for the news section
5. **Medium blog integration** from `https://medium.com/@getnetdemil` (live, so new posts auto-appear)
6. **FlowCV resume embed** from `https://flowcv.com/resume/pwg1rj0mti`
7. **Better theme** — not extra dark background with gray/unreadable text
8. **List all social media** from old website and include them
9. **Google Scholar**: `https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Xz_tNToAAAAJ&hl=en`
10. **LinkedIn**: `https://www.linkedin.com/in/getnetdemil/`

---

2. Key Technical Concepts:
- Pure static HTML/CSS/JS (GitHub Pages compatible, no build tools)
- "Nordic Midnight" upgraded color system (WCAG AA compliant — raised backgrounds from `#050c1a` to `#0a1628`, new `--color-text-body: #c8daf0` variable at ~7:1 contrast)
- "Aurora Rail" timeline — animated gradient vertical line using `background-size: 100% 300%` + `@keyframes railPulse` CSS animation; items use `opacity:0; transform:translateX(-12px)` → `.tl-item--visible` via IntersectionObserver with inline `--delay` CSS custom property for stagger
- Category-colored timeline dots via CSS custom property `--category-color` set by `data-category` attribute on `.tl-item`
- News section tabs (Highlights / Blog Posts) using ARIA `role="tabpanel"` / `role="tab"` with `hidden` attribute toggling
- Medium RSS live feed via `https://api.rss2json.com/v1/api.json?rss_url=https://medium.com/feed/@getnetdemil` (free CORS-enabled RSS-to-JSON proxy)
- Universal "See More / Collapse" pattern driven by `data-see-more="N"` attribute on containers
- FlowCV iframe embed with CSS fallback (`flowcv-wrap--error` class added on iframe error event)
- LinkedIn: No public API — handled with a "Follow on LinkedIn" CTA card appended to Medium feed
- Semantic Scholar API for live citation count
- IntersectionObserver for both timeline animations and general fade-in
- CSS Custom Properties dual-theme (`data-theme="dark"` / `data-theme="light"`)
- Footer social icon strip (10 icons, 32×32 circle links)
- 10-card contact grid (5-col desktop → 3-col tablet → 2-col mobile)
- `requestAnimationFrame` ease-out cubic counter animation
- `history.replaceState` URL hash fix

---

3. Files and Code Sections:

**`/scratch/gdemil24/getnet-demil.github.io/css/style.css`**
- Complete redesign of color system (dark theme variables), all prose text references changed to `--color-text-body`, news section CSS replaced, new CSS blocks appended
- Key changes:
```css
/* NEW Nordic Midnight dark theme */
:root, [data-theme="dark"] {
  --color-bg:            #0a1628;   /* was #050c1a */
  --color-bg-alt:        #0d1c34;
  --color-surface:       #132238;
  --color-surface-2:     #1a2d4a;
  --color-surface-3:     #203556;
  --color-text:          #e8f2ff;
  --color-text-body:     #c8daf0;   /* NEW — primary prose ~7:1 contrast */
  --color-text-muted:    #94b4d4;   /* was #7a9abd — now 5.1:1 */
  --color-text-faint:    #4e6e90;
  --color-border:        rgba(255,255,255,0.09);
  --color-border-strong: rgba(255,255,255,0.16);
}

/* Aurora Rail timeline */
.news-timeline::before, .tl-group-items::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; left: 20px; top: 8px; bottom: 8px; width: 2px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-primary) 0%, var(--color-purple) 45%, var(--color-accent) 85%, var(--color-primary) 100%);
  background-size: 100% 300%;
  animation: railPulse 8s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes railPulse { 0% { background-position: 0% 0%; } 50% { background-position: 0% 100%; } 100% { background-position: 0% 0%; } }

.tl-item {
  position: relative; padding-left: 56px; margin-bottom: 28px;
  opacity: 0; transform: translateX(-12px);
  transition: opacity 0.45s ease var(--delay, 0ms), transform 0.45s ease var(--delay, 0ms);
}
.tl-item--visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0); }

/* Category color mapping */
.tl-item[data-category="conference"]  { --category-color: var(--color-primary); }
.tl-item[data-category="publication"] { --category-color: var(--color-accent); }
.tl-item[data-category="workshop"]    { --category-color: var(--color-purple); }
.tl-item[data-category="visit"]       { --category-color: #60a5fa; }
.tl-item[data-category="education"]   { --category-color: var(--color-accent); }
.tl-item[data-category="position"]    { --category-color: var(--color-primary); }

/* FlowCV */
.flowcv-frame-wrap { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 700px; }
.flowcv-iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; }
.flowcv-wrap--error .flowcv-fallback { display: flex; }
.flowcv-wrap--error .flowcv-iframe   { display: none; }

/* See More */
.see-more-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; padding: 10px 26px; border-radius: var(--radius-full); ... }
.see-more-icon { transition: transform var(--transition); }

/* Contact grid: 5-col → 3-col → 2-col */
.contact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 14px; }
@media (max-width: 900px) { .contact-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 640px) { .contact-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }

/* Footer social strip */
.footer-social-link { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; width:32px; height:32px; border-radius:50%; border:1px solid var(--color-border); ... }
```

**`/scratch/gdemil24/getnet-demil.github.io/js/main.js`**
- Complete rewrite with all new functions
- Key code:
```javascript
// Medium RSS Feed
(function initMediumFeed() {
  var container = document.getElementById('mediumFeed');
  if (!container) return;
  var RSS = 'https://medium.com/feed/@getnetdemil';
  var API = 'https://api.rss2json.com/v1/api.json?rss_url=' + encodeURIComponent(RSS) + '&count=10';
  // ... renders .medium-card elements, appends LinkedIn CTA card
  // Falls back to error message if fetch fails
})();

// News Tabs
(function initNewsTabs() {
  var tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.news-tab');
  var panels = document.querySelectorAll('[role="tabpanel"]');
  tabs.forEach(function (tab) {
    tab.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var target = tab.getAttribute('data-tab');
      tabs.forEach(function(t) { t.classList.remove('active'); t.setAttribute('aria-selected','false'); });
      tab.classList.add('active'); tab.setAttribute('aria-selected','true');
      panels.forEach(function(panel) { panel.hidden = (panel.id !== 'tab-' + target); });
    });
  });
})();

// Universal See More
(function initSeeMore() {
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-see-more]').forEach(function (container) {
    var max = parseInt(container.getAttribute('data-see-more'), 10);
    var items = Array.from(container.children);
    var wrap = container.nextElementSibling;
    var btn = wrap && wrap.classList.contains('see-more-wrap') ? wrap.querySelector('.see-more-btn') : null;
    var hidden = items.slice(max);
    if (!btn || !hidden.length) { if (wrap && wrap.classList.contains('see-more-wrap')) wrap.hidden = true; return; }
    hidden.forEach(function(el) { el.hidden = true; });
    btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      var isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      hidden.forEach(function(el) { el.hidden = isOpen; });
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!isOpen));
      if (icon) icon.style.transform = isOpen ? '' : 'rotate(180deg)';
    });
  });
})();

// Timeline animations with stagger
var tlObserver = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
  entries.forEach(function(entry) {
    if (entry.isIntersecting) { entry.target.classList.add('tl-item--visible'); tlObserver.unobserve(entry.target); }
  });
}, { threshold: 0.1 });
document.querySelectorAll('.tl-item').forEach(function(el, i) {
  el.style.setProperty('--delay', (i % 5) * 80 + 'ms');
  tlObserver.observe(el);
});
```

