- "as an initial its perfect. but it need a lot of redesigning and content wise issues. please visit the old website to understand everything getnetdemil.github.io / extract all the informations from there, make butiful timeline design for news, for education and carrer sections. you can have a smart see more like button to see all the details for long section. / for the news section think to integrate or render or directly take linkedin posts to the website. and also the blogs should be from my medium account (i will post blogs in medium so that it will be showed up in the website) https://medium.com/@getnetdemil / linkedin https://www.linkedin.com/in/getnetdemil/ / scholarly google https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Xz_tNToAAAAJ&hl=en / my resume or cv must be redered from https://flowcv.com/resume/pwg1rj0mti and like that. / the themes of the website must be appealing to watch or visit. dont make it extra dark background and gray texts (not readable) / list all social media listed in the old website" [main redesign request]

---

7. Pending Tasks:
- **Git commit and push** the completed redesign to GitHub. All three files have been written but NOT yet committed.
- Verify FlowCV iframe actually loads in browser (may need testing)
- Verify Medium RSS feed loads correctly via rss2json API

---

8. Current Work:
All three files for the v2 redesign were just completed immediately before this summary request:

1. **`css/style.css`** — fully updated with Nordic Midnight colors, Aurora Rail timeline CSS, news tabs, Medium feed cards, FlowCV embed, See More buttons, footer socials, 10-col contact grid, all responsive breakpoints

2. **`js/main.js`** — complete rewrite with: `initMediumFeed()` (rss2json API), `initNewsTabs()`, `initSeeMore()` (universal `data-see-more` handler), timeline IntersectionObserver with stagger delays, FlowCV error handler

3. **`index.html`** — complete rewrite (~950+ lines) with: correct Scholar ID `Xz_tNToAAAAJ`, 5-button hero (Scholar, GitHub, ResearchGate, LinkedIn, University), news section with Highlights/Blog tabs + aurora rail timeline + see-more, projects grid with data-see-more="3", publications with fixed SIGIR DOI (`10.1145/3769733.3769737`), CV section with FlowCV iframe + 3 tl-group sections (Research & Positions, Research Visits with RISE Sweden + UF TREC, Education), 10-card contact grid (Email, GitHub, LinkedIn, Scholar, ORCID, ResearchGate, Medium, Twitter/X, Instagram, University), footer with 10-icon social strip

