# Plan: Full Redesign — Getnet Demil Portfolio (v2)

## Context
The initial build at `/scratch/gdemil24/getnet-demil.github.io/` works structurally but has three categories of problems the user wants fixed:
1. **Readability** — `#050c1a` background + `#7a9abd` muted text fails WCAG AA contrast (≈3.2:1). Too much body text uses the muted variable.
2. **Design gaps** — News section is a flat grid, CV is a featureless list, no expand/collapse on long sections.
3. **Content gaps** — wrong Scholar ID, 4 social media links missing, Research Visits not shown, no Medium blog feed, no FlowCV embed.

---

## Files to Modify
- `index.html`
- `css/style.css`
- `js/main.js`

---

## 1. New Color System — "Nordic Midnight" (readable dark)

Replace the entire `:root, [data-theme="dark"]` block:

```css
--color-bg:            #0a1628;   /* was #050c1a — lifted 3 stops */
--color-bg-alt:        #0d1c34;
--color-surface:       #132238;
--color-surface-2:     #1a2d4a;
--color-surface-3:     #203556;
--color-text:          #e8f2ff;   /* brighter near-white */
--color-text-body:     #c8daf0;   /* NEW — primary prose (~7:1 on bg) */
--color-text-muted:    #94b4d4;   /* was #7a9abd — now 5.1:1 */
--color-text-faint:    #4e6e90;
--color-border:        rgba(255,255,255,0.09);
--color-border-strong: rgba(255,255,255,0.16);
--color-card-bg:       rgba(19,34,56,0.90);
```

Add `--color-text-body` variable to every prose paragraph: `.about-text p`, `.news-desc`, `.tl-body`, `.timeline-desc`, `.pub-authors`, `.pub-venue`, `.project-card-desc`, `.project-card p`, `.highlight-card p`, `.medium-excerpt`.

Also update hardcoded rgba values in navbar scrolled (line ~300) and mobile nav overlay (line ~1454) from `rgba(5,12,26,...)` → `rgba(10,22,40,...)`.

---

## 2. Navigation — Keep 8 items, no change

`About | News | Research | Projects | Publications | CV | Service | Contact`

Research Visits go into CV section. Blog/Medium goes into News section as a sub-tab. No new nav item needed.

---

## 3. News Section — Timeline + Tabs

Replace the current `.news-grid` two-column card layout with:

**Two tabs:** "Highlights" (static news, from HTML) and "Blog Posts" (live Medium RSS).

**Timeline structure** (Highlights tab):
```html
<div class="news-tabs" role="tablist">
  <button class="news-tab active" data-tab="highlights">Highlights</button>
  <button class="news-tab" data-tab="blog">Blog Posts <span id="mediumBadge"></span></button>
</div>

<div id="tab-highlights" role="tabpanel">
  <ol class="news-timeline" data-see-more="4">
    <li class="tl-item" data-category="conference">...</li>
    <!-- 6 items total -->
  </ol>
  <div class="see-more-wrap">
    <button class="see-more-btn" data-label-more="Show all news" data-label-less="Show less">
      Show all news <svg class="see-more-icon">chevron-down</svg>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>

<div id="tab-blog" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  <div id="mediumFeed" class="medium-feed">
    <div class="medium-loading"><span class="spinner"></span> Loading…</div>
  </div>
</div>
```

**tl-item structure** (shared between News and CV):
```html
<li class="tl-item" data-category="publication" style="--delay:0ms">
  <div class="tl-marker"><div class="tl-dot"></div></div>
  <time class="tl-date" datetime="2025-01">Jan 2025</time>
  <div class="tl-card">
    <span class="tl-cat">Publication</span>
    <p class="tl-headline">Title here</p>
    <p class="tl-body">Description here</p>
  </div>
</li>
```

**Category → color mapping** (via CSS custom property):
```css
.tl-item[data-category="conference"]  { --category-color: var(--color-primary); }
.tl-item[data-category="publication"] { --category-color: var(--color-accent); }
.tl-item[data-category="workshop"]    { --category-color: var(--color-purple); }
.tl-item[data-category="visit"]       { --category-color: #60a5fa; }
.tl-item[data-category="award"]       { --category-color: #f87171; }
.tl-item[data-category="position"]    { --category-color: var(--color-primary); }
.tl-item[data-category="education"]   { --category-color: var(--color-accent); }
```

---

## 4. "Aurora Rail" Timeline CSS (for News + CV)

A new CSS block replaces the old `.news-grid`, `.news-card`, and `.timeline` styles:

```css
/* Rail */
.news-timeline::before, .tl-group::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 20px; top: 8px; bottom: 8px; width: 2px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-primary) 0%, var(--color-purple) 45%, var(--color-accent) 85%, var(--color-primary) 100%);
  background-size: 100% 300%;
  animation: railPulse 8s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes railPulse { 0% { background-position: 0% 0%; } 50% { background-position: 0% 100%; } 100% { background-position: 0% 0%; } }

/* Item — initially hidden, revealed by IntersectionObserver */
.tl-item {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 56px;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateX(-12px);
  transition: opacity 0.45s ease var(--delay,0ms), transform 0.45s ease var(--delay,0ms);
}
.tl-item--visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0); }

/* Dot */
.tl-dot {
  position: absolute;
  left: 13px; top: 18px;
  width: 14px; height: 14px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--color-bg);
  border: 2.5px solid var(--category-color, var(--color-primary));
  z-index: 1;
  transition: box-shadow .3s, transform .3s;
}
.tl-item--visible .tl-dot { box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(0,200,180,0.15); }
.tl-item:hover .tl-dot { transform: scale(1.3); }

/* Card */
.tl-card {
  padding: 18px 22px;
  background: var(--color-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  border-left: 3px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  transition: border-left-color .22s, transform .22s, background .22s, box-shadow .22s;
}
.tl-item:hover .tl-card {
  border-left-color: var(--category-color, var(--color-primary));
  transform: translateX(4px);
  background: var(--color-surface-2);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
}
.tl-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .71rem; color: var(--color-primary); margin-bottom: 7px; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; display: block; }
.tl-cat  { font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .09em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--category-color, var(--color-primary)); margin-bottom: 5px; display: inline-block; }
.tl-headline { font-size: .94rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text); line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 5px; }
.tl-body { font-size: .855rem; color: var(--color-text-body); line-height: 1.6; }

/* Group labels (CV only) */
.tl-group { position: relative; }
.tl-group-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text); margin: 0 0 24px 56px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
.tl-group + .tl-group { margin-top: 48px; }
```

Mobile: `--tl-gutter: 36px`, `--tl-rail-x: 12px` at 640px.

---

## 5. CV Section Restructure

Replace the current single `<div class="timeline">` with:
1. **FlowCV iframe block** (top of section)
2. **Three `tl-group` divs:** Research & Positions | Research Visits | Education

Each group uses `data-see-more="3"` on its items wrapper + a `see-more-wrap`.

### FlowCV block:
```html
<div class="flowcv-wrap">
  <div class="flowcv-header">
    <h3>Interactive CV</h3>
    <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href="https://flowcv.com/resume/pwg1rj0mti" target="_blank">Open Full CV</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="https://flowcv.com/resume/pwg1rj0mti/download" target="_blank">Download PDF</a>
  </div>
  <div class="flowcv-frame-wrap">
    <iframe src="https://flowcv.com/resume/pwg1rj0mti" class="flowcv-iframe" loading="lazy" title="CV"></iframe>
  </div>
</div>
```
Frame height: 680px desktop, 420px mobile.

### Research Visits group (new — currently missing):
- RISE Sweden, Gothenburg — Jan–Feb 2026 (multi-task DL for Nordic snow; Erasmus+ Grant badge)
- University of Florida TREC — Jun–Jul 2026 (multi-sensor drone fusion)

### Extra CV badges to add:
- IPCV Erasmus Mundus timeline item → add `IPCV Excellence Scholarship` badge
- BSc item → already has Best Project badge ✓

---

## 6. See More Pattern (universal)

One shared JS function driven by `data-see-more="N"` attribute on the container + a `.see-more-wrap` sibling.

```javascript
(function initSeeMore() {
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-see-more]').forEach(function (container) {
    var max = parseInt(container.getAttribute('data-see-more'), 10);
    var items = Array.from(container.children);
    var wrap = container.nextElementSibling;
    var btn = wrap && wrap.querySelector('.see-more-btn');
    var icon = btn && btn.querySelector('.see-more-icon');
    var hidden = items.slice(max);
    if (!btn || !hidden.length) { if (wrap) wrap.hidden = true; return; }
    hidden.forEach(function(el){ el.hidden = true; });
    btn.addEventListener('click', function(){
      var open = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      hidden.forEach(function(el){ el.hidden = open; });
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!open));
      if (icon) icon.style.transform = open ? '' : 'rotate(180deg)';
      if (!open && hidden[0]) hidden[0].scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'nearest'});
    });
  });
})();
```

Sections that get `data-see-more`:
- `#tab-highlights .news-timeline` → `data-see-more="4"`
- `#projects .projects-grid` → `data-see-more="3"`
- Each CV `tl-group` items wrapper → `data-see-more="3"`

---

## 7. Medium RSS Feed

**Service:** `https://api.rss2json.com/v1/api.json?rss_url=https://medium.com/feed/@getnetdemil&count=10`

JS IIFE renders into `#mediumFeed` as a `medium-feed` grid (2 cols desktop, 1 col mobile). Each `.medium-card` shows: date, read-time estimate, title (linked), 140-char excerpt, "Read on Medium →" link. Appends a LinkedIn CTA card at end. Shows a spinner while loading, graceful empty-state fallback.

Tab switching JS (another IIFE): toggles `hidden` attribute on tabpanels, updates `aria-selected` on tab buttons.

---

## 8. Social Media Fixes

### Fix Scholar ID everywhere (3 places):
`https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Xz_tNToAAAAJ&hl=en`

### Add missing social links (4 new):
- Twitter/X: `https://twitter.com/getnetdemil`
- Instagram: `https://www.instagram.com/getnet_demil_jr/`
- ResearchGate: `https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Getnet-Jenberia`
- Medium: `https://medium.com/@getnetdemil/`

### Contact grid: expand to 10 cards (5-col desktop, 3-col tablet, 2-col mobile)
Email · GitHub · LinkedIn · Scholar · ORCID · Medium · ResearchGate · Twitter/X · Instagram · University

### Footer: add `.footer-socials` strip of 10 icon-only circle links

### Hero buttons: add ResearchGate + Twitter/X as ghost buttons (keeping primary=Scholar, outline=GitHub)

---

## 9. Publications — Fix DOI + Scholar URL

- SIGIR DOI: change to `https://doi.org/10.1145/3769733.3769737`
- Scholar CTA URL: fix with real ID

---

## 10. JS Changes Summary

`js/main.js` additions (IIFEs in this order, at top):
1. Semantic Scholar fetch (existing — fix query if needed)
2. `initMediumFeed()` — RSS via rss2json
3. `initNewsTabs()` — tab switching
4. `initSeeMore()` — universal expand/collapse

`fadeObserver` selector: add `.tl-item, .medium-card` — but timeline items use `.tl-item--visible` class, not `.visible`. Add a separate IntersectionObserver for `.tl-item` elements that adds `.tl-item--visible` (with stagger delay from `--delay` inline var).

---

## Verification

1. Dark mode: body prose text should be visibly bright, not dark gray
2. News tabs: click "Blog Posts" → spinner → Medium post cards render
3. "Show all news" button → hidden items reveal with smooth scroll
4. CV section: FlowCV iframe loads; if blocked, fallback link shows
5. Research Visits group visible in CV with RISE + UF TREC entries
6. Scholar links all resolve to real profile
7. Contact grid shows 10 cards
8. Footer shows 10 social icons
9. All 8 nav links scroll to correct sections
10. Mobile: hamburger menu works, timeline readable, iframe collapses to 420px

